 (verdict Inconclusive)
 (notes
  "NOT LIVE as written (rule step 1), so the pre-registered return rule was not applied: Inconclusive; not escalated; Price_band_seeded stays a default-off axis; no default changes. Had liveness passed, the rule would read INCONCLUSIVE (median max DD P 31.20 vs S 25.56 = +5.64 pp > 3, the #3588 QC reading), not ESCALATE. The proxy was mis-specified: on the 2,011 Friday-pairs both arms recorded, the top-20 differs on 67 % (1.4 names/Friday; S-not-P 86 % >= $33, P-not-S 94 % < $33) and 21.5 % of P's tickets are not placed by S that Friday; the order mainly demotes >= $33 (59.3 % -> 51.7 % of entries) for $14-33; no price cut-off reaches 1.3 x (max 1.219 at $14). Descriptive only: delta ln(1+R) +0.563/+0.210/+0.421/+0.348/+0.143 (median +0.348), every P seed above every S seed (about 2-2.4 SD under a shared-draw bound, one-sided p ~0.01-0.02; 1/252 and the 1/32 sign test are floors because the five P cells share one fixed cross-band order), Sharpe 5/5 higher, Ulcer 5/5 higher. WHY: shared positions earn the same; the gap is the one-arm 21-27 %, a fatter tail at a lower win rate (P-only p90 +33.6 % vs +19.7 %, >= +100 % 2.3 % vs 0.4 %); ~70 % from 2010-12 entries (MERC $6.39 +111 %, ATML, WAL, DINO, REGN: P 4-5 seeds vs S 0-1) plus ADMA 2023-08-18 (P 5/5 vs S 3/5, +300 %); 2018-23 negative 5/5. The order is seed-invariant across bands, so seeds replicate the same ~5 names; effective n is small and the trait was found on the same history. FORWARD: first one S cell with --emit-candidates (exact binding rate on one path + the breakout sub-gate that drops low-priced monsters, the larger leak: 50.6 % of < $8 monsters vs 33.6 % > $33); only then, if warranted, a fresh pre-registration with a liveness bar from that rate, a fixed DD reading, a name-concentration check and broad-vs-broad confirmation cells (2013-2026 sub-window, top-1000 schedule), K=5 paired each. Writeup: dev/experiments/price-band-tiebreak-2026-11-13/README.md §Results."))
